What does this program print? Assume `fork()` succeeds and output appears immediately.

```c
int x = 5;
int main(void) {
    if (fork() == 0) {
        x += 5;
        printf("%d ", x);
    } else {
        wait(NULL);
        x -= 2;
        printf("%d ", x);
    }
    return 0;
}
```

